afk: task.isolation.requireCow — plumb the reflink strictness knob from
settings to the backend.

Motivation: with omp-reflink-degraded-copy.patch (applied in the natives
build) the pinned reflink backend silently degrades to a byte copy on
filesystems without FICLONE (ext4: measured 6.6x clone wall time, 178x
on-disk cost on a 1.3 GB repo). Hosts where that cost should be an error
rather than a shrug — and hosts that want to catch a filesystem
regression, e.g. ZFS losing block cloning — set
task.isolation.requireCow: true to restore the hard failure. Default
false; per-host override via ~/.omp/config.yml layers above the distro
config.

What must survive a rebase:
- Settings schema: "task.isolation.requireCow" boolean, default false,
  Isolation UI group — and the SAME key in main.ts
  HOST_DEFAULTED_SETTING_PATHS (omitting it lets RPC/ACP startup clobber
  explicit caller/project config; upstream CHANGELOG documents that bug
  class for the sibling keys).
- Plumb: structured-subagent reads the setting into
  runIsolatedSubprocess opts; IsolatedRunOptions.requireCow;
  ensureIsolation(repoRoot, id, preferred?, requireCow = false) passes
  `requireCow ? { requireCow: true } : null` as isoStart's 4th argument.
  worktree.ts itself never reads settings — callers resolve and pass
  primitives (same contract as preferredBackend).
- Semantics: requireCow makes the reflink backend return
  ISO_UNAVAILABLE instead of degrading; combined with the pinned-backend
  patch (candidates = [preferred]) that fails the spawn loudly. Under
  auto mode the resolver may still walk to the next backend — requireCow
  constrains the reflink backend, not the resolver.
- Tests: worktree.test.ts asserts the options object reaches
  natives.isoStart ({ requireCow: true } when set, null otherwise); the
  pure-jj snapshot test's exact-args assertion carries the 4th `null`.

Rebased 18.1.13 -> 18.2.10: the pruned isolation-runner test hunks are
gone; the jj e2e test (test/task/vcs-jj-e2e.test.ts, from
omp-jj-workspace-handle) passes requireCow: false.

